cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as follows:"
title: "HCP MRI-Based Perivascular Space (PVS) Analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Salesi
    given-names: Razieh
version: 1.0.0
abstract: >
  Python-based image-processing workflows for MRI-based perivascular
  space (PVS) analysis using T1-weighted, T2-weighted, and enhanced
  perivascular contrast (EPC) images from the Human Connectome Project.
  The repository includes modality-specific processing pipelines,
  quantitative PVS measurements, visualization, and statistical analysis.
keywords:
  - Perivascular spaces
  - Glymphatic system
  - MRI
  - Medical image processing
  - Human Connectome Project
  - Neuroimaging
  - Python